      "properties": {
        "entityId": "wu",
        "startDate": "0195-08-01",
        "endDate": "0196-12-31",
        "order": 3,
        "segmentType": "advance",
        "name": {
          "zh": "历阳—曲阿—吴—会稽（孙策定江东）",
          "en": "Liyang–Qua–Wu–Kuaiji (Sun Ce takes the Lower Yangtze)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "兴平二年（195）孙策自历阳渡江，先破横江、当利，转战牛渚、秣陵，进至曲阿击走刘繇；建安元年（196）破吴郡严白虎，随即引兵渡浙江攻会稽，王朗据固陵抵抗，孙策用孙静之计夜出查渎、突袭高迁屯，王朗败走东冶后投降。孙策自领会稽太守，以朱治为吴郡太守。原线止于吴，线尾无后续；此处补会稽一段。",
          "en": "In 195 Sun Ce crossed the Yangtze at Liyang, took Hengjiang and Dangli, fought through Niuzhu and Moling and drove Liu Yao from Qua. In 196 he defeated Yan Baihu in Wu commandery, then crossed the Zhejiang against Kuaiji; Wang Lang held Guling until Sun Ce, on Sun Jing’s advice, made a night feint and struck Gaoqian tun, routing Wang Lang, who fled to Dongye and surrendered. Sun Ce took the title of Kuaiji governor and made Zhu Zhi governor of Wu. The former line ended at Wu with no follow-through; the Kuaiji leg is now added."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
