        "order": 19,
        "segmentType": "counterattack",
        "name": {
          "zh": "寻阳—公安—江陵（吕蒙白衣渡江）",
          "en": "Xunyang–Gong’an–Jiangling (Lu Meng’s plain-clothes crossing)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "建安二十四年（219）关羽北伐、后方空虚，吕蒙称病还建业，陆逊代屯陆口以骄关羽；关羽撤兵后，吕蒙自寻阳率精兵伏于船中，使白衣摇橹作商贾，昼夜兼行，尽收江边屯候，遂袭公安、江陵，傅士仁、糜芳先后投降，关羽后方尽失。原线起点作陆口，实际出兵地为寻阳；此处改正。寻阳取今九江一带代表点，标 approx。",
          "en": "In 219, with Guan Yu away on his northern campaign and his rear thinly held, Lu Meng feigned illness and returned to Jianye while Lu Xun took over at Lukou to lull Guan Yu. Once Guan Yu withdrew his troops, Lu Meng set out from Xunyang with picked men hidden in the ships, disguised the rowers as merchants and moved day and night, sweeping up the riverbank watch posts and seizing Gong’an and Jiangling as Fu Shiren and Mi Fang surrendered in turn, stripping Guan Yu of his rear. The former line began at Lukou, but the actual starting point was Xunyang; this is now corrected. Xunyang is represented by the Jiujiang area and marked approx."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic",
          "locationPrecision": "approx"
        }
