      "properties": {
        "entityId": "wu",
        "startDate": "0228-08-01",
        "endDate": "0228-09-30",
        "order": 24,
        "segmentType": "counterattack",
        "name": {
          "zh": "皖口—石亭（陆逊迎击曹休）",
          "en": "Wankou–Shiting (Lu Xun meets Cao Xiu)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "黄武七年（228）八月孙权至皖口，以陆逊为大都督，朱桓、全琮为左右督，各督三万人迎击曹休；陆逊自为中部，三道俱进，追至夹石，斩获万余。皖口为皖水入江之口，即今安庆市大观区山口乡山口镇村，距安庆城十五华里；原坐标置于今望江、太湖之间，偏西约 50 公里，已改正。石亭地望在今潜山东北（一说怀宁或桐城境），暂取潜山代表点。路线为示意。",
          "en": "In the eighth month of 228 Sun Quan reached Wankou and made Lu Xun commander-in-chief, with Zhu Huan and Quan Cong as left and right commanders, each with 30,000 men against Cao Xiu; Lu Xun took the centre, advanced in three columns, pursued to Jiashi and killed or captured over 10,000. Wankou, where the Wan river enters the Yangtze, is Shankou village in modern Anqing’s Daguan district, 15 li west of the city; the former coordinate lay between Wangjiang and Taihu, some 50 km to the west, and has been corrected. Shiting is placed north-east of modern Qianshan (some accounts put it in Huaining or Tongcheng), using Qianshan as a representative point. The line is schematic."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
